# Touch Grass 🌿 — Environment Variables Example
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY NOTICE (read this first)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend variables prefixed with VITE_ are INLINED into the client-side
# JavaScript bundle during `npm run build` and are PUBLIC. Anyone can read them.
#
#   ⛔ NEVER put a private API key in a VITE_ variable.
#   ⛔ NEVER commit a .env file that contains a real secret.
#
# Two safe ways to use AI in Touch Grass:
#
#   1. Local / personal use (simplest)
#      Open the "Open-Source AI Settings" modal in the app and paste your key.
#      It is stored ONLY in your browser's localStorage and is never sent to us.
#      No .env file is required for this.
#
#   2. Hosted / production use (recommended for public deployments)
#      Add a serverless function (see api/ai-proxy.js), set the real key as a
#      SERVER-side variable there, and point the client at the proxy with the
#      non-secret VITE_AI_PROXY_URL below. The browser never receives the key.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Client-side (NON-SECRET) configuration ───────────────────────────────────
# Optional. When set, AI requests are routed through your secure serverless
# proxy (api/ai-proxy.js) which injects the private key server-side.
# Example for Vercel: /api/ai-proxy
# VITE_AI_PROXY_URL=/api/ai-proxy

# Optional: Local Ollama inference on localhost (no secret involved)
VITE_OLLAMA_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:11434
VITE_DEFAULT_OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# Optional: Remote OpenAI-compatible endpoint base URL (NON-SECRET)
VITE_REMOTE_API_ENDPOINT=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
VITE_DEFAULT_REMOTE_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant

# ── Server-side ONLY (used inside api/ai-proxy.js — NEVER prefix with VITE_) ──
# Configure these in your hosting provider's environment settings, not in a
# VITE_ variable, and never commit real values.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_google_ai_studio_key_here
# REMOTE_API_KEY=your_openai_compatible_key_here
# Optional SSRF allowlist for the remote endpoint (comma separated):
# AI_PROXY_ALLOWED_ENDPOINTS=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
